pra: 0194 - the touch panel init in the COMPILED arm (the -1,-1 fix)

THE BOOTED KERNEL PROVED THE ROOT CAUSE (work/ci193/dl, T17 kernel
cc83d49c): the PRA compile line defines BOTH -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_PRA
and -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE (work/ci193/fail/build.log:34742), so
SweetHIDTouch::start() is compiled with the A5XELTE arm (the const pool
@0x702e720 holds 1080,1920,0,0). 0193 added fPanelW/fPanelH ONLY to the
#else arm; in the compiled arm start() never stores them (the
disassembly has no str to [x19,#0xc0]/[x19,#0xc4]) and they stay zero.
touch() then clamps with `x >= fPanelW ? fPanelW - 1 : x`; fPanelW = 0
subtracts 1 into -1, so every real coordinate became -1,-1 - exactly
ring58: "PRA touch: hid inject slot=0 down x=550 y=1911" followed by
"SWEET HID: touch 0 down at -1,-1 edge".

THIS PATCH (0194):
1. Initialize fPanelW/fPanelH in BOTH arms. The compiled A5XELTE arm is
   the PRA panel: 1080x1920 (pra_touch.c PANEL_X_MAX/PANEL_Y_MAX, and
   the framebuffer swaps 1080x1920), logical 1080x1920, zero offsets.
2. Publish the working A5 board's real 68x121 mm in that arm. 0193 made
   SurfaceWidth unconditional 8655995 (132.08 mm) from treating the
   5.2-inch diagonal as the width; the #else arm keeps 132x144 mm.
3. One-time marker "SWEET HID: panel arm" in the compiled arm so a
   silently skipped 0194 fails the CI strings guard.

The falsifier (next pratouchreset=1 boot): SWEET HID touch lines carry
the real injected coordinates (e.g. 550,1911) instead of -1,-1, and the
UI reacts. Still -1,-1 = the compiled arm differs from this source;
real coords but no UI = the next rung is userland routing.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
@@ -441,10 +441,27 @@
 	}
 	int native = 0;
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_native", &native, sizeof(native));
+	/*
+	 * 0194: BOTH ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_PRA and ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE
+	 * are on the PRA compile line, so THIS arm is the one that runs on
+	 * PRA. 0193 added fPanelW/fPanelH only to the #else arm, leaving
+	 * them zero here - the panel clamp then turned every real touch
+	 * into (-1,-1). Initialize the panel in BOTH arms.
+	 * PRA's panel is 1080x1920 (pra_touch.c PANEL_X_MAX/PANEL_Y_MAX
+	 * and the framebuffer's 1080x1920 swaps), the same geometry as the
+	 * working A5 board, so publish that board's real 68x121 mm.
+	 */
+	int surfaceWmm, surfaceHmm;
+
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE)
+	fPanelW = 1080;
+	fPanelH = 1920;
 	fLogicalW = 1080;
 	fLogicalH = 1920;
 	fOffX = fOffY = 0;
+	surfaceWmm = 68;	/* the 1080x1920 panel's real ~68x121 mm */
+	surfaceHmm = 121;
+	IOLog("SWEET HID: panel arm A5XELTE 1080x1920\n");
 #else
 	fPanelW = 1080;	/* the PRA panel (the framebuffer's native) */
 	fPanelH = 2400;
@@ -452,19 +469,17 @@
 	fLogicalH = native ? 2400 : 2436;
 	fOffX = (fLogicalW - fPanelW) / 2;
 	fOffY = (fLogicalH - fPanelH) / 2;
+	surfaceWmm = 132;
+	surfaceHmm = 144;
 #endif
 	/* The digitizer covers the main display (backboardd maps it 1:1). */
 	setProperty("DisplayIntegrated", kOSBooleanTrue);
-	setProperty("SurfaceWidth", (unsigned long long)(8655995ull), 32);	/* mm, 16.16 - the PRA panel: 5.2 in x 25.4 */
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE)
-	setProperty("SurfaceHeight", (unsigned long long)(121 << 16), 32);
-#else
-	setProperty("SurfaceHeight", (unsigned long long)(9422111ull), 32);	/* mm, 16.16 - 2400 px / 424 ppi x 25.4 */
-#endif
+	setProperty("SurfaceWidth", (unsigned long long)((unsigned)surfaceWmm << 16), 32);	/* mm, 16.16 */
+	setProperty("SurfaceHeight", (unsigned long long)((unsigned)surfaceHmm << 16), 32);
 	gSweetTouch = this;
 	registerService();
 	IOLog("SWEET HID: surface %ux%u mm panel %ux%u\n",
-	    8655995 >> 16, 9422111 >> 16, fPanelW, fPanelH);
+	    surfaceWmm, surfaceHmm, fPanelW, fPanelH);
 	IOLog("SWEET HID: touch registered\n");
 	return true;
 }
